<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Barcelona</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">878–1410</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a> was the dynasty of counts of Barcelona descended from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilfred-the-hairy">Wilfred the Hairy</a>, who gathered several Catalan counties under one line in the late 9th century. By the marriage of Ramon Berenguer IV and Petronilla in 1137 it acquired the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-aragon">Kingdom of Aragon</a> and ruled the Crown of Aragon until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-of-aragon">Martin the Humane</a> died in 1410.</p></div>
